# Changelog ownership (multi-repo)

When a task changes documentation, tooling, or config, add a changelog row in the **owning** repository only. Do not duplicate the same change across multiple changelogs.

## Canonical map

| Repository | Changelog | Owns |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| GitLab `cursor-test` | `admin-guide/Cursor-Docs-Changelog.md` | User/Admin guides, NAC, Michu/Trundle, dashboards, docs-as-code workflow, `scripts/`, CI, `AGENTS.md` |
| ParaDOCS plugin | Changelog section in `docs/ParaDOCS-Plugin-Overview.md` | Plugin packaging, local install, bundled rules/skills, plugin operator docs |
| Paragon Knowledge | Changelog section in `docs/Paragon-Knowledge-MCP-Overview.md` | MCP tools/Apps UI, corpora wiring, convert/OCR scripts that feed the MCP, MCP operator docs |
| Technical Documentation | `CHANGELOG.md` | `paradocs.py`, convert tooling, corpus pipeline, ParaDOCS app settings |

## Anti-duplication

1. One logical change → **one** row in the owning changelog.
2. Cross-cutting work (for example a plugin rename that also needs a User Guide sentence) → one row per **owning surface** only. Do not copy the same "What changed" text into a second changelog.
3. Prefer linking across docs ("see overview §6") over restating the same history in two tables.
4. Do not edit the ADO `CursorAI` / `CursorAI-2` mirror for changelog or content. ADO is read-only and overwritten by the GitLab mirror.
5. Ignore `node_modules/**` and `michu/snapshots/**` when searching for changelogs.

## Format by owner

| Owner | Format |
| :--- | :--- |
| `cursor-test` | UK date `## DD-MM-YYYY` sections; table with Area, What changed, Link, sync_id, sync_repo, request_form_ids, michu, Why. See `changelog-cursor-docs.mdc`. |
| Plugin repo (ParaDOCS) | UK date `### DD-MM-YYYY` under the Changelog section in `docs/ParaDOCS-Plugin-Overview.md`; same table columns and `pending` `sync_id`. |
| Plugin repo (Paragon Knowledge) | Same format under the Changelog section in `docs/Paragon-Knowledge-MCP-Overview.md`. |
| Technical Documentation | Keep a Changelog format with ParaDOCS version headings from `VERSION` in `paradocs.py`. Match existing subheadings and voice in that file. |

## Required behavior

1. Before adding a row, confirm which repo (and which product overview, on the plugin repo) owns the files you changed.
2. If no meaningful change occurred, state that no changelog update is required.
3. When editing on `cursor-test`, follow `changelog-cursor-docs.mdc` for Area routing and row format.
